                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 658.119/457</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-20T17:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 20, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received June 22, 12.30 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2342. In reference to my 2308, June 15, 5 p.m. and 2309, June 15, 6 p.m. Swedish
                    Government is awaiting written reply from the Associated Governments that the
                    agreement as ratified by Sweden is satisfactory. The Italian Minister has
                    received word from his Government that same is satisfactory but to wait
                    informing the Swedish Government until the other Allied representatives here did
                    the same. The British Minister received word from his Government that the
                    agreement having been signed in England with full powers by their delegates, no
                    further action on their part is necessary after ratification by Swedish
                    Government and has so informed the Swedish Foreign Minister. I am therefore
                    awaiting authority from you regarding this matter and would call to your
                    attention that the Swedish Government has been expecting to hear from me.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
